      "origin": "suggested",
      "teacherReviewRequired": true,
      "markedParagraph": "God told [Moses] to send [twelve] men into [Canaan]. The spies explored the land for [forty] days. They brought back a large bunch of [grapes] and reported that the land was good. But [ten] spies spread a fearful report about the strong people and walled cities. The Israelites wanted to return to [Egypt]. [Caleb] and [Joshua] urged the people to trust God. The frightened crowd threatened them, and God’s [glory] appeared at the Tabernacle. Moses asked God to [forgive] the people. Because they refused to trust God, the Israelites would [wander] in the wilderness for forty years."
    },
